", "lead_before": -21.91, "lead_after": -21.88, "points_lost": 0.03, "best": "C7"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "A Level Start, Then the Wall Gave Way", "summary": "The 20k won as White when GPT-6.1 Sol resigned after 46 moves. The game was close at the start (Black's lead was -1.2 after move 10), but GPT-6.1 Sol's 6.8-point loss at move 11 began a slide. More losses at moves 19, 25 and 27 stretched the deficit to -19.7. The 20k made two blunders of its own, but each time Black gave back more than it gained.", "moments": [{"turn": 11, "text": "GPT-6.1 Sol's F5 dropped Black's lead from -1.2 to -8.0, a loss of 6.8 points. The engine preferred G6. It was the first big swing of the game, and the position never really settled afterwards."}, {"turn": 12, "text": "The 20k answered with H7, which lost 6.7 points and moved Black's lead from -8.0 back to -1.3. The engine wanted G7. For one move the game was almost even again."}, {"turn": 15, "text": "GPT-6.1 Sol played C3, losing 5.0 points and taking the lead from -5.6 to -10.6. The engine's choice was C4. The 20k's wall in the centre kept growing from here."}, {"turn": 19, "text": "C5 lost 7.6 points as Black's lead went from -3.5 to -11.1. The engine preferred C7. GPT-6.1 Sol had just been handed a chance to recover and gave the points straight back."}, {"turn": 27, "text": "F4 was GPT-6.1 Sol's worst move, losing 9.8 points and taking the lead from -9.9 to -19.7. The engine's first choice was H3. After this the lead stayed near -20 until the end, and GPT-6.1 Sol resigned."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "The `inspect` function (stored in command 4) only flood-fills the current board for chains, liberties and empty regions, and applies one named move to compute its captures. The `act` wrapper, the replay check in command 29, and the file writes are record-keeping, and every move was chosen by hand with no looping over candidates or look-ahead.", "stop": false}}